CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
GITHUB_TOKEN=
ZERO_RTT_REPO_PATH=
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS=
TELEGRAM_HOME_CHANNEL=

# Do NOT set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here. Anthropic auth resolves
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -> ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN -> OAuth token, so a stray key wins
# over everything else and silently switches this profile to per-token billing.

# Do NOT add AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, AWS_SESSION_TOKEN, or
# AWS_PROFILE to this file. Stack state is read through GitHub Actions' OIDC role.
# A credential here would give the warden the power to destroy the thing it is
# only supposed to report on.

# OPENROUTER_API_KEY is load-bearing on this profile: the warden exists to break
# silence about a running stack, so it must degrade to the fallback rather than
# die on a 429. Leaving it blank turns the warden into the failure it guards.

# GITHUB_TOKEN scope: actions:write + contents:read on ofekm5/zero-rtt-tcp.
# Caveat worth knowing: actions:write cannot be narrowed to a single workflow
# input, so this token technically permits `action=destroy`. The status-only
# limit lives in SOUL.md and config.yaml, not in the token. Use a token distinct
# from the runner's so the two can be revoked independently.
